# DEFECT 2558, beside it: a call to address zero the library before the
# runtime declines is still told (2026-11-15).
#
# The arm for a call through a null function pointer names its fault by the
# address alone, as the null read's arm does, so it asks the handler before
# the runtime's first in the same place, and tells the call when that handler
# gives it back unchanged. Under `--sanitize` AddressSanitizer reports it
# (`fixedbugs-2558-library.h`).

extern "fixedbugs-2558-library.h"
    function lib_call_declined() -> i64

function main()
    print("before")
    print(lib_call_declined())
